/* =============================================================================
 * EVO PLAYER PRO - Dev debug overlay (menu FPS pill)
 *
 * GL-5 (#81) moved the dev FPS readout into the player OSD (#fps-pill in
 * playback.rml) and dropped the menu case. This restores it for every
 * non-player screen: a tiny fixed pill in its OWN Rml::Context, composited on
 * top of whatever menu is underneath - the same pattern toast.rcss uses - so
 * it never disturbs the RenderCachedScreen surface cache. Visibility + the
 * number are pushed from C++ (EvoRmlApp::UpdateDebugOverlay), gated on the
 * Settings -> System -> "Debug Overlay" toggle (show_debug_overlay).
 * Matches the old draw_fps_overlay position (top-right, 12dp inset) and the
 * player #fps-pill style.
 * ============================================================================= */

body {
    font-family: LatoLatin;
    font-weight: normal;
    font-size: 15dp;
    color: #f8fafc;
    background-color: transparent;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 1920dp;
    height: 1080dp;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
}

div, span {
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

#debug-pill {
    position: absolute;
    top: 12dp;
    right: 12dp;
    background-color: #000000aa;
    border-radius: 6dp;
    padding: 4dp 10dp;
    z-index: 9;
}

#debug-fps {
    font-size: 15dp;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #f8fafc;
    letter-spacing: 0.5dp;
}
